From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] modem-daemon: find a call on the modem that has it
Description:
 Accepting, hanging up and sending DTMF tones looked the call up only on
 the modem the client named. With several modems the client does not know
 the modem of an incoming call or passes none, and the request was dropped
 ("deviceUni not found"). Call paths are unique among all modems: look the
 call up on the named modem first, then on every modem.
Forwarded: no
License: LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
